% Claims across policies, run through the whole model (dmepos_all.le): a
% power wheelchair with a cushion, a CPAP with concurrent oxygen.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base all cases includes these resources:
    dmepos_all.

the knowledge base all cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

% A CPAP (initial criteria met) and a concentrator for the same beneficiary:
% both reasonable and necessary under their own policies.
scenario cpap_and_oxygen is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ann.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    Ann received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    claim 2 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Ann.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the arterial PO2 of Ann taken at rest is 54 mm Hg.
    the blood gas study of Ann was performed by treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Ann.
    the blood gas study of Ann was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A CPAP claim complete but for the proof of delivery, through the whole
% model: it fails at the remedy, whichever other policies are loaded.
scenario cpap_no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    Ann received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    the order for the CPAP device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the CPAP device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the CPAP device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the CPAP device includes order date.
    the order for the CPAP device includes description of the item.
    the order for the CPAP device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the CPAP device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the CPAP device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% A power wheelchair complete but for the home assessment, through the whole
% model: it fails at the remedy (pmd.le's own documentation rule).
scenario pmd_no_home_assessment is:
    claim 1 is for the power wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the power wheelchair is "K0823".
    the power wheelchair is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding scooter ruled out about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Ann is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Ann is 180 pounds.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the power wheelchair in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the power wheelchair is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the power wheelchair is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the power wheelchair includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the power wheelchair includes order date.
    the order for the power wheelchair includes description of the item.
    the order for the power wheelchair includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the power wheelchair includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the power wheelchair was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the order for the power wheelchair was written by the practitioner who conducted the face-to-face encounter.
    prior authorization for the power wheelchair was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the power wheelchair was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the power wheelchair.

    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
